  <subsection xml:id="subsec-LearningTargets">
    <title>Learning Targets (LTs)</title>

    <p>
      Here is a list of the 22 LTs for this course. Most will only be referred to by number 
      (as in, "This week's quiz will cover LTs #12, 13 and 14.") so you will need to refer to this list frequently.
    </p>

    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add, subtract, multiply, and divide fractions.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Evaluate and simplify expressions using the order of operations.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Evaluate numbers and simplify expressions involving exponents, absolute values, and square roots.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Locate numbers on the number line and answer questions about their relative positions.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Solve linear equations with whole number coefficients.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Solve linear equations involving fractions.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Evaluate formulas at given values and solve them for a given variable.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Solve word problems by setting up and solving an equation.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Simplify expressions using various properties of exponents.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add and subtract polynomials.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Multiply polynomials, including squaring a binomial.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Divide polynomials by a monomial.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Identify the greatest common factor (GCF) of a polynomial, and factor it from a polynomial.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Use factoring by grouping to completely factor a polynomial.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Factor trinomials of the form <m>x^2+bx+c</m>, including ones with GCFs.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Factor a difference of squares, including ones with GCFs.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Solve quadratic equations using the zero-product property and factoring.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Simplify a rational expression completely.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Multiply and divide rational expressions, and simplify completely.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add and subtract rational expressions with like denominators, and simplify completely.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Find the lowest common denominator (LCD) for rational expressions, and use them to add and subtract rational expressions with unlike denominators.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Solve rational equations.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    
  </subsection>
</section>
